---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { SITE_TITLE, EDITOR } from '../consts';
---

<Layout title="Colophon" description={`How ${SITE_TITLE} is made.`}>
	<p class="kicker">Colophon</p>
	<h1>How this is set</h1>

	<div class="prose">
		<p>
			<strong>{SITE_TITLE}</strong> is a personal digital magazine by {EDITOR}. Every issue
			is written in Markdown and published as a static site.
		</p>

		<h2>Reading an issue</h2>
		<p>
			An issue is one long page — every article in it, stacked, divided by a heavy rule
			and a numbered masthead. A floating <em>Index</em> in the corner opens a full-screen
			table of contents; pick a piece and it scrolls you there. The archive keeps the
			back issues.
		</p>
		<h2>The typesetting</h2>
		<p>
			Each article also has its own page, and there it offers a second mode. The default
			is plain semantic HTML. Switch to <em>magazine</em> and the same text is re-set onto
			a <code>&lt;canvas&gt;</code> by{' '}
			<a href="https://github.com/chenglou/pretext">pretext</a>, a text-measurement and
			line-breaking library that does its own layout instead of relying on the browser.
		</p>
		<p>
			That buys things the browser will not give you: a real multi-column flow that
			paginates, body text that narrows around a drop cap and widens again past it,
			pull-quotes and inset figures that text wraps around, and headlines fitted to
			exactly the width of the page.{' '}<code>layoutNextLineRange</code>{' '}accepts a
			different maximum width on every single line, which is the whole trick.
		</p>

		<h2>The look</h2>
		<p>
			Printed — on screen — in two spot inks, acid yellow and medium blue, over black on
			newsprint. Each ink is drawn on its own layer and stamped back slightly out of
			register, the way a Risograph misaligns its drums. There is a grain plate on top.
			Photographs are reduced to a single ink.
		</p>
		<p>
			Display type is <strong>Syne</strong>; body is <strong>Space Grotesk</strong>;
			folios and labels are <strong>Space Mono</strong>.
		</p>

		<h2>Colours</h2>
		<ul class="swatches">
			<li style="--c:#F2EDE0">Newsprint · #F2EDE0</li>
			<li style="--c:#FFEC4D">Acid yellow · #FFEC4D</li>
			<li style="--c:#0E5AD6">Medium blue · #0E5AD6</li>
			<li style="--c:#22201C">Black · #22201C</li>
		</ul>
	</div>
</Layout>

<style>
	h1 {
		font-size: clamp(2.5rem, 9vw, 5rem);
		margin-bottom: 2rem;
	}
	.prose {
		max-width: var(--measure);
		font-size: 1.05rem;
		line-height: 1.7;
	}
	.prose h2 {
		margin-top: 2.2em;
		color: var(--ink);
		font-size: 1.4rem;
		width: fit-content;
		padding: 0.05em 0.15em;
		background: linear-gradient(var(--pink), var(--pink)) 0 100% / 100% 0.4em no-repeat;
	}
	.prose p {
		margin: 0 0 1.2em;
	}
	.swatches {
		list-style: none;
		padding: 0;
		display: grid;
		gap: 0.5rem;
		font-family: var(--font-mono);
		font-size: 0.8rem;
	}
	.swatches li {
		display: flex;
		align-items: center;
		gap: 0.75rem;
	}
	.swatches li::before {
		content: '';
		width: 2rem;
		height: 2rem;
		background: var(--c);
		border: 2px solid var(--ink);
	}
</style>
